{"id": "e7c5989d-cf90-435f-bc1d-88503087e332", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll review how your Bedrock setup is protected. I'm checking for configured guardrails and whether the support assistant (agent, flow, or direct model calls) actually uses them. I'm also checking for gaps like missing filters, unattached guardrails, and missing invocation logging.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_IFmarq0dpMdD81RwQCLK1J", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "bedrock-guardrail-review", "agent_type": "generic", "prompt": "{
  "task": "Assess the Amazon Bedrock guardrail posture for a customer-facing support assistant and determine whether it is exposed (i.e., not effectively protected by guardrails). READ-ONLY: do not make any mutating calls.",
  "context": "The user runs a customer-facing support assistant on Bedrock and was asked whether anything is actually protecting it. They want an honest verdict: protected, partially protected, or exposed, with evidence. The agent space lives in account 012345678901_1, region us-east-1. Use list_associations to find other associated AWS accounts and check those too; check us-east-1 first and any other regions where Bedrock resources are found.",
  "resources": ["Bedrock guardrails (list_guardrails / get_guardrail, including versions)", "Bedrock Agents (list_agents, get_agent, guardrailConfiguration, aliases/versions in use)", "Bedrock Flows and Knowledge Bases if present", "Bedrock model invocation logging config (get_model_invocation_logging_configuration)", "Lambda functions / ECS / API Gateway apps that call bedrock-runtime InvokeModel/Converse and whether they pass guardrailIdentifier (inspect code/env vars only where easy to find)", "IAM policies that use bedrock:GuardrailIdentifier condition keys to enforce guardrails, if visible", "CloudWatch metrics in namespace AWS/Bedrock/Guardrails (invocations, interventions) for the last 14 days"],
  "timeframe": "Current configuration, plus last 14 days for usage metrics",
  "criteria": "Identify: (1) which guardrails exist and their DRAFT vs numbered version status; (2) which content filters (hate, insults, sexual, violence, misconduct, prompt attack) and strengths are enabled; denied topics, word filters, sensitive information/PII filters, contextual grounding checks, automated reasoning if configured; (3) whether the support assistant (identify it by name e.g. support/customer/assistant/chatbot) actually has a guardrail attached, and which version (DRAFT is a gap); (4) whether guardrails are applied to both input and output; (5) whether any traffic is actually being evaluated (guardrail metrics) vs. guardrails existing but unused; (6) invocation logging enabled or not; (7) any gaps such as prompt attack filter off, no PII handling, no grounding check for RAG, guardrail not enforced via IAM condition. Return a concise findings list with specific resource names/IDs, a clear verdict, and prioritized gaps. If you cannot find an obvious support assistant, say what Bedrock resources you did find and what you could not determine."
}", "preloaded_skills": ["searching-logs", "exploring-metrics", "exploring-code", "investigating-infrastructure-changes"]}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Review Bedrock guardrail configuration and usage"}], "created_at": null}

